    tease: 'Before the yard, Dutch Okonkwo ran the day shift at the Harlow heavy works. Harlow went bankrupt eleven years ago and locked the gate. Nobody thought to switch off the night shift, which is automatic, and which has been building pilotless machines ever since and stacking them in the yard with their lights out. The Red Maw has found the yard. They have three code vans waking the machines one at a time. Dutch has never asked the company for anything. He is asking.',
    wire: 'Lights seen at the old Harlow works, shut these eleven years. The Free League says squatters. The yard chief of a certain mercenary company says he knows exactly what it is, and has gone very quiet.',
